WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.095
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.395 --> 00:00:08.700
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:16.784
Unit twenty-five: Review: Leading Change. Today you will say what you want others to do with 'want + object + to + verb'.

4
00:00:17.084 --> 00:00:19.655
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.891
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:25.438
Change.

7
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:28.798
Change means something becoming different.

8
00:00:29.383 --> 00:00:31.731
Small actions can create big change.

9
00:00:32.317 --> 00:00:34.737
Your turn. Say: Change.

10
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:38.497
Change.

11
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:40.019
Leader.

12
00:00:41.017 --> 00:00:43.086
Leader means a person who guides a group.

13
00:00:43.683 --> 00:00:45.323
A good leader listens.

14
00:00:45.917 --> 00:00:48.546
Your turn. Say: Leader.

15
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.297
Leader.

16
00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:53.958
Initiative.

17
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:57.902
Initiative means a new plan to solve a problem.

18
00:00:58.517 --> 00:01:01.213
Our recycling initiative started last month.

19
00:01:01.817 --> 00:01:04.423
Your turn. Say: Initiative.

20
00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:08.256
Initiative.

21
00:01:09.017 --> 00:01:09.762
Vision.

22
00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:13.539
Vision means a clear idea of the future you want.

23
00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:16.533
Her vision is a plastic-free school.

24
00:01:17.117 --> 00:01:19.572
Your turn. Say: Vision.

25
00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:23.318
Vision.

26
00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:24.910
Teamwork.

27
00:01:25.917 --> 00:01:27.986
Teamwork means working well together.

28
00:01:28.583 --> 00:01:30.827
Teamwork made the project a success.

29
00:01:31.417 --> 00:01:33.744
Your turn. Say: Teamwork.

30
00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:37.404
Teamwork.

31
00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:39.116
Impact.

32
00:01:40.117 --> 00:01:42.163
Impact means a strong effect.

33
00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:44.668
The campaign had a big impact.

34
00:01:45.283 --> 00:01:47.576
Your turn. Say: Impact.

35
00:01:50.433 --> 00:01:51.504
Impact.

36
00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:53.286
Community.

37
00:01:54.283 --> 00:01:57.188
Community means the people who live in one area.

38
00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:59.713
Our community cleaned the river.

39
00:02:00.317 --> 00:02:03.004
Your turn. Say: Community.

40
00:02:05.867 --> 00:02:06.845
Community.

41
00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:08.515
Action.

42
00:02:09.517 --> 00:02:11.435
Action means something you do.

43
00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:14.456
It's time for action, not just words.

44
00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:17.261
Your turn. Say: Action.

45
00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.020
Action.

46
00:02:21.833 --> 00:02:25.322
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.183 --> 00:02:28.415
Visal, what change would you like to lead?

48
00:02:29.517 --> 00:02:31.481
I want people to recycle more.

49
00:02:32.583 --> 00:02:33.817
How will you start?

50
00:02:34.917 --> 00:02:38.565
I want my classmates to join a recycling initiative.

51
00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:40.756
What is your vision?

52
00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:46.093
A clean community. I want everyone to take action together.

53
00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:48.594
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:53.365
Grammar focus: Want plus object plus to plus verb.

55
00:02:53.665 --> 00:02:54.817
Look at the pattern.

56
00:02:55.517 --> 00:02:57.400
I want people to recycle more.

57
00:02:58.317 --> 00:03:00.630
Our teacher wants us to lead the project.

58
00:03:01.517 --> 00:03:03.806
I want my community to plant more trees.

59
00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:12.017
Say 'want' + person + 'to' + verb. Don't say 'want that people…'. Use object pronouns: me, you, him, her, us, them.

60
00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:16.772
Be careful! Don't say: I want that people recycle more.

61
00:03:18.733 --> 00:03:21.743
Say: I want people to recycle more.

62
00:03:22.043 --> 00:03:24.635
Say 'want' + person + 'to' + verb.

63
00:03:25.433 --> 00:03:27.993
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:29.906
Be the Change.

65
00:03:30.206 --> 00:03:34.202
This year, we learned about confidence, empathy and responsibility.

66
00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.211
Now it is time to lead change.

67
00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.977
A good leader has a vision and starts an initiative.

68
00:03:41.967 --> 00:03:44.895
Leaders want everyone to work with teamwork and respect.

69
00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.991
I want my community to take action and make an impact.

70
00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.811
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.708
I want people blank recycle more.

72
00:03:57.008 --> 00:03:59.999
A, to. B, that. C, for.

73
00:04:03.533 --> 00:04:05.150
The answer is A: to.

74
00:04:06.283 --> 00:04:08.863
A clear idea of the future you want is a blank.

75
00:04:09.163 --> 00:04:12.527
A, vision. B, change. C, community.

76
00:04:16.067 --> 00:04:17.706
The answer is A: vision.

77
00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:20.699
Working well together is blank.

78
00:04:20.999 --> 00:04:24.315
A, teamwork. B, initiative. C, impact.

79
00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:29.959
The answer is A: teamwork.

80
00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:34.376
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:35.217 --> 00:04:36.938
What change would you like to lead?

82
00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:47.169
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:47.469 --> 00:04:55.218
I would like to lead a reading club in my village. I want children to love books, and I want parents to read with them every night.

84
00:04:55.518 --> 00:04:57.181
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:04:58.083 --> 00:05:03.336
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and want plus object plus to plus verb.

86
00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:08.495
Today's value is leadership. Lead fairly, listen to others and set a good example.

87
00:05:08.795 --> 00:05:15.060
Congratulations! You have finished Online B two, Book two. See you in Online B two, Book three!

88
00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:19.115
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

